1
00:00:17,647 --> 00:00:23,647
The news if finally worth reporting.

2
00:00:35,294 --> 00:00:41,294
Dixie Times is a drama film directed by Sherrie Peterson.

3
00:00:52,941 --> 00:00:58,941
A moonshiner turned sheriff's deputy helps bring in
the bad guys armed with duct tape.

4
00:01:10,588 --> 00:01:16,588
The local newspaper reporter now has some major events to write about, and a sleepy
little Alabama farming community is making the news all over Dixie.

5
00:01:28,235 --> 00:01:34,235
Briscoe Tanner, played by Ken R. Wheeler.

6
00:01:45,882 --> 00:01:51,882
Alice Bentley, played by Stacey Turner.

7
00:02:03,529 --> 00:02:09,529
Michael Bradley, played by Chad Fishburne.

8
00:02:21,176 --> 00:02:27,176
Clifford Scruggs, played by Dan Mengini.

9
00:02:38,823 --> 00:02:44,823
Horace Shaw, played by Justin Welborn.

10
00:02:56,470 --> 00:03:02,470
Louis, played by Chris Burns.

11
00:03:14,117 --> 00:03:20,117
Because of Winn-Dixie is a 2005 American comedy-drama film based on Kate DiCamillo's 2000 novel of the same name,
with the screenplay written by Joan Singleton, produced by Trevor Albert and directed by Wayne Wang.

12
00:03:31,764 --> 00:03:37,764
The film was produced by Walden Media and released by 20th Century Fox.

13
00:03:49,411 --> 00:03:55,411
Because of Winn-Dixie stars Jeff Daniels, Cicely Tyson, Eva Marie Saint,
Dave Matthews and AnnaSophia Robb in her feature film debut.

14
00:04:07,058 --> 00:04:13,058
It premiered at the USA Film Festival on January 26, 2005, and
was theatrically released on February 18, 2005.

15
00:04:24,705 --> 00:04:30,705
The film received mixed reviews from critics and earned $33.5
million against a production budget of $14 million.

16
00:04:42,352 --> 00:04:48,352
It was released on DVD and VHS on August 9, 2005 by
20th Century Fox Home Entertainment.
